From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] binder: use EINTR for interrupted wait for work

When a signal interrupts a thread that waits for work in
binder_wait_for_work(), return -EINTR instead of -ERESTARTSYS. The
BINDER_WRITE_READ ioctl is then no longer restarted by the kernel when
there is no signal handler or the handler has SA_RESTART; userspace sees
EINTR and repeats the call itself. libbinder and libhwbinder do
(IPCThreadState::talkWithDriver(): "} while (err == -EINTR);"), and they
always had to, for handlers installed without SA_RESTART.

This is the third patch of the upstream freezer series and the behaviour
of every kernel since 5.13, which is what current Android userspace is
developed against. The other patches of this series do not depend on it
and it can be left out on its own: on this kernel the threads that wait
here are marked PF_FREEZER_SKIP (freezer_do_not_count()), so the
freezers do not send them their fake signal and only real signals
interrupt the wait.

Derived from upstream:
  95c16f9d9cf9 "binder: use EINTR for interrupted wait for work"

Applies as upstream.

Compile-tested (GCC 4.9, lineage_gts210ltexx_defconfig); not run on the
device.
---
 drivers/android/binder.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/android/binder.c b/drivers/android/binder.c
index 47c0cba4..2450f609 100644
--- a/drivers/android/binder.c
+++ b/drivers/android/binder.c
@@ -4077,7 +4077,7 @@ static int binder_wait_for_work(struct binder_thread *thread,
 		binder_inner_proc_lock(proc);
 		list_del_init(&thread->waiting_thread_node);
 		if (signal_pending(current)) {
-			ret = -ERESTARTSYS;
+			ret = -EINTR;
 			break;
 		}
 	}
@@ -5181,7 +5181,7 @@ err:
 	if (thread)
 		thread->looper_need_return = false;
 	wait_event_interruptible(binder_user_error_wait, binder_stop_on_user_error < 2);
-	if (ret && ret != -ERESTARTSYS)
+	if (ret && ret != -EINTR)
 		pr_info("%d:%d ioctl %x %lx returned %d\n", proc->pid, current->pid, cmd, arg, ret);
 err_unlocked:
 	trace_binder_ioctl_done(ret);
